21:19:26 [890f] - advanced conjunction (More complex conjunction structures): e.g. while, although, before, after
21:19:26 [890f] - auxiliary verbs (Helping verbs): e.g. is, are, was, were, has, have
21:19:26 [890f] - copula verbs (Linking verbs): e.g. is, am, are, was, were
21:19:26 [890f] - verb tense concepts (Past, present, future, and progressive tense usage): e.g. I play, I played, I will play, I am playing
21:19:26 [890f] - causal explanation language (Language forms used to explain cause-effect relationships.): e.g. because, so, if...then, that happened because...
21:19:26 [890f] - narrative sequence language (Language forms used to organize story events and sequences.): e.g. first, then, next, after that, finally
21:19:26 [890f] - perspective taking language (Language forms used to discuss thoughts, feelings, beliefs, and perspectives.): e.g. he thinks, she feels, they know, I wonder, maybe
21:19:26 [890f] 
21:19:26 [890f] Practise these target speech sounds by naturally featuring words that contain them (do not turn the story into a pronunciation drill):
21:19:26 [890f] - advanced sounds [th, r, ch] (Late-developing speech sounds for articulation practice.): e.g. thumb, three, rabbit, red, chair, cheese
