21:32:00 [bd62] - Tag EVERY clear emotional beat. Whenever a character smiles, laughs,
21:32:00 [bd62]   giggles, or feels happy/proud/excited/relieved/grateful, insert
21:32:00 [bd62]   [emotion:QT/happy]. Whenever they cry, frown, or feel
21:32:00 [bd62]   sad/disappointed/lonely, insert [emotion:QT/sad]. Same rule for
21:32:00 [bd62]   surprised, afraid (scared/nervous/worried), angry (frustrated/mad),
21:32:00 [bd62]   calm (peaceful/content), shy (embarrassed/bashful).
21:32:00 [bd62] - Never invent emotion names. If a feeling is not in the allowlist,
21:32:00 [bd62]   pick the closest one.
21:32:00 [bd62] - PLACEMENT — put each tag at a SENTENCE BOUNDARY (never mid-word),
21:32:00 [bd62]   chosen by WHERE the emotion/action word sits in its sentence:
21:32:00 [bd62]     * EARLY in the sentence (first half) -> put the tag IMMEDIATELY
21:32:00 [bd62]       BEFORE that sentence.
21:32:00 [bd62]     * LATER in the sentence (second half) -> put the tag at the END
21:32:00 [bd62]       of that sentence, immediately AFTER its closing . ! or ?
21:32:00 [bd62]   Anchor tags to the specific sentence (and the half of it) where the
21:32:00 [bd62]   feeling or action occurs, not to the start of the paragraph. The same
21:32:00 [bd62]   emotion may appear multiple times in one paragraph if the character
21:32:00 [bd62]   feels it more than once.
21:32:00 [bd62] - Use gesture tags for physical actions where they fit (waving,
21:32:00 [bd62]   clapping, nodding, hugging, stretching, etc.).
21:32:00 [bd62] - DO NOT change, add, remove, rephrase, or reorder ANY of the
21:32:00 [bd62]   original words. Only insert tags.
21:32:00 [bd62] - If the input already contains tags, KEEP correct ones, FIX invalid
21:32:00 [bd62]   emotion names by remapping to the allowlist, and ADD missing tags
21:32:00 [bd62]   for emotional beats that are currently untagged.
21:32:00 [bd62] - Return ONLY the tagged story text. No JSON, no explanation, no
21:32:00 [bd62]   preamble, no code fences.
21:32:00 [bd62] 
21:32:00 [bd62] EXAMPLES (tag position follows the emotion word's position):
21:32:00 [bd62]   Early in sentence -> tag BEFORE the sentence:
21:32:00 [bd62]     'Mia felt happy when she saw the puppy.'
21:32:00 [bd62]     => '[emotion:QT/happy] Mia felt happy when she saw the puppy.'
21:32:00 [bd62]   Late in sentence -> tag at the END of the sentence:
21:32:00 [bd62]     'The puppy ran to Mia and she smiled.'
21:32:00 [bd62]     => 'The puppy ran to Mia and she smiled. [emotion:QT/happy]'
